IV. Recently implemented:

(2.a has been implemented and transfered to project history, and remains for context only)
2.a EX system overhaul: untangle rules & declarations from the ex hierarchy, so ex tree can be moved to models without losing sight of functionality from core. (Preparatory step for import revamp)
    [x] 'clanker.py', 'BaseEx' decoupled from ex hierarchy, transformed to convenience class for centralization of ex system rules and declarations.
        - Rename 'BaseEx' to 'ExceptionPolicy'
        - it no longer enforces the rule that no non-leaf nodes are allowed to instantiate.
        - other functionality and declarations remain as-is

    [x] 'clanker.py', 'models.py': migrate ex declarations to models.
        - redeclare 'BaseEx' in models:
                BaseEx(ABC, Exception)
                    @abstractmethod 
                    leaf_ex(self):pass #guards instantiations for it and downstream inheritors
        - move 'Failure(BaseEx)', 'ControlNotice(BaseEx)' and 'UserNotice(BaseEx)' to models
            - they dont override leaf_ex, so they cannot be instantiated.
        - move remaining ex classes to models. they must all override is_leaf to allow their instantiation.
        - this combines to give us some rather nice semantics:
            - class Failure(BaseEx): pass
            - class MissedNotice(Failure): leaf_ex = True

